# =============================================================================
# pre-push — the guard at the gate
# =============================================================================
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
# - Runs by itself every time you type "git push", BEFORE anything leaves
#
# WHY IMPORTANT:
# - Isolation is the promise Rahisisha stands on. A broken lock must never
#   reach GitHub
#
# DANGER (if this file does not exist):
# - A push with a broken tenant lock goes through and nobody notices
#
# WHAT IT SOLVES:
# - You can forget to run the tests. The computer cannot
#
# SYSTEM DESIGN PRINCIPLE:
# - Automate the check you might forget
#
# RULES:
# - Never push with --no-verify. That bribes the guard to look away
# - If this fails, fix the lock. Do not edit this file to make it pass
# =============================================================================

# Go into the API folder, then run the isolation tests.
# If any test fails, npm exits with an error and git CANCELS the push
cd apps/api && npm run test:isolation